~ vorkoth_transformation_intro
# Vorkoth stumbles, breathing hard. The crowd goes quiet.

vorkoth_p1: (laughing, low) You actually landed a few. I'll admit — didn't expect that.

vorkoth_p1: Guess I'll stop holding back, then.
=> END

~ vorkoth_transformation_reveal
# A dark, fire-veined energy erupts from Vorkoth. His form twists, growing, splitting — the humanoid mask cracking into something else entirely. (the screen fade + actual phase-2 swap happens in code, between the intro and reveal dialogue sections)

NPCCrowdVoice1: (from the audience, horrified) It's — it's true, then. He really is one of them.

NPCCrowdVoice2: (from the audience) All this time...

vorkoth_p2: (voice distorted, guttural) THIS is what it takes to lead. THIS is what real strength looks like. Not whatever it is you four think you're doing.

astryn: (steadying herself) ...Right. Guess we do this the hard way.
=> END

~ vorkoth_defeat
# Vorkoth collapses, the monstrous form flickering weakly, half-reverted. The crowd roars — no longer afraid, no longer silent.

# Astryn doesn't move yet. She glances back at the team — all of them worn ragged, breathing hard, weapons hanging low like they're too heavy to lift again. No one steps forward to stop her. Spero leans against his staff, jaw tight, arms crossed. Aegrandir, chest still heaving, gives the smallest nod.

# Novius steps up beside Astryn instead of staying back. Their eyes meet for half a second — no words needed, just a shared, exhausted understanding of exactly what this man is.

vorkoth_p2: (weak, human voice bleeding back through) ...heh. Didn't think you had it in you.

astryn: Give it up. Step down. Give back what you've stolen from this city, and maybe — maybe — these people find it in them to forgive you.

vorkoth_p2: (a weak, humorless laugh) Forgive me. For what — running this city the only way it's ever worked?

vorkoth_p2: I'd do it again. Every coin, every tariff, every debt I called in. This city breathes because I make it breathe. Take that away and watch how fast it starves without me.

novius: (quiet, cold) You know how many times I said no to people who couldn't pay? Watched their faces when I did it — telling myself it wasn't my fault, that it was just how things worked. I still see that look on this whole city every time you open your mouth.

vorkoth_p2: (contemptuous, even now) Then you understand. Someone has to make the hard calls. I just made mine honestly — I didn't dress it up as kindness like you did.

astryn: That's not power. That's just theft with a title.

vorkoth_p2: Call it whatever lets you sleep at night. I built something here. You just want to burn it down and call it justice.

vorkoth_p2: Go on, then. Everyone's watching. Let's see what you really are underneath all that talk.

# Astryn walks toward him slowly. Novius doesn't stop her — doesn't even move. She reaches down through the slit of her dress, drawing a pistol from a holster strapped to her thigh — a weapon she never uses in battle. She racks the slide, chambering a round, and raises it, level with his head.

vorkoth_p2: (a flicker of genuine surprise) ...That's not your style.

astryn: (small, humorless smile) Special occasion, asshole.

- Spare Vorkoth => vorkoth_spare_check
- Kill Vorkoth => vorkoth_kill

# Routes to the Novius-intervenes version of sparing him if Astryn and Novius bonded
# earlier (dialogue_novius.dialogue's ~ novius_followup node), otherwise the normal
# (fatal) spare outcome.
~ vorkoth_spare_check
if QuestManager.novius_bonded == true:
	=> vorkoth_spare_novius_intervenes
=> vorkoth_spare

~ vorkoth_kill
astryn: (barely a whisper) ...For justice.

# A single gunshot cracks through the arena. Vorkoth drops.

# Cut to black.

